        "original_id": "120ca59d-8488-5538-9392-459352ef4a87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Victor Garber, Teri Copley, Robert C. Hughes, Andrew Stevens, John Matuszak\n- TV series: I Had Three Wives, We Got It Made, Alias\n- Films: Down the Drain, Titanic, Argo\n- Stage productions: Godspell, Assassins, Lend Me a Tenor\n- Roles: Jesus, Anthony Hope, John Wilkes Booth, Jack Bristow, Max, Thomas Andrews, Ken Taylor\n\nFacts:\n- In 1983, Teri Copley appeared on the American NBC/syndicated television series \"We Got It Made,\" which premiered that year.\n- In 1985, Teri Copley co-starred on the CBS television series \"I Had Three Wives.\"\n- Victor Garber was the lead of \"I Had Three Wives,\" and it was his first starring role on television.\n- Victor Garber is known for playing Jesus in \"Godspell,\" Anthony Hope in \"Sweeney Todd,\" John Wilkes Booth in \"Assassins,\" Jack Bristow in the television series \"Alias,\" Max in \"Lend Me a Tenor,\" Thomas Andrews in James Cameron's \"Titanic,\" and Ken Taylor in \"Argo.\"\n- The film \"Down the Drain\" was directed by Robert C. Hughes and starred Andrew Stevens, Teri Copley, and John Matuszak.\n- \"Down the Drain\" was John Matuszak's last film and was released after his death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
